WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.731 --> 00:05.569 align:center line:79%
Last June, a terrible accident occurred
in the country of Lesotho

00:05.569 --> 00:06.837 align:center line:81%
in southern Africa.

00:08.138 --> 00:13.277 align:center line:79%
A small bus carrying twenty young women
of the Maputsoe Branch of the Church

00:14.011 --> 00:18.015 align:center line:79%
and seven of their leaders
was headed to the capital city, Maseru,

00:18.682 --> 00:21.385 align:center line:79%
for a gathering of young
women from their district.

00:22.719 --> 00:25.923 align:center line:79%
As they traveled the two-lane highway
in the morning hours,

00:26.156 --> 00:30.994 align:center line:79%
a car coming in the opposite direction,
attempting to pass another vehicle,

00:31.762 --> 00:34.131 align:center line:81%
came into the lane occupied by the bus.

00:35.132 --> 00:38.835 align:center line:79%
There was no space or time
to avoid a head-on collision,

00:39.670 --> 00:42.706 align:center line:79%
and within seconds the
vehicles hit, rolled

00:42.706 --> 00:45.609 align:center line:81%
off the road, and burst into flames.

00:46.877 --> 00:52.349 align:center line:79%
In all, fifteen people died in the
accident, including six young women,

00:52.983 --> 00:57.287 align:center line:79%
two Young Women leaders,
and the branch president and his wife.

00:58.355 --> 01:02.926 align:center line:79%
Survivors, family members, and friends
have expressed a range of emotions,

01:02.926 --> 01:06.830 align:center line:79%
including moments of anger,
and depression, even guilt.

01:07.864 --> 01:10.667 align:center line:79%
Despite these feelings
and unanswered questions,

01:10.667 --> 01:16.039 align:center line:79%
they have comforted one another
and turned to God through sacred music,

01:16.673 --> 01:20.844 align:center line:79%
the scriptures, and prayer,
where they have found solace.

01:22.012 --> 01:25.549 align:center line:79%
Seventeen-year-old survivor
Setso’ana Selebeli

01:25.582 --> 01:29.219 align:center line:81%
testified, “Jesus Christ loves us

01:29.219 --> 01:33.056 align:center line:79%
and is with us, even
though our hearts hurt.”

01:34.791 --> 01:36.093 align:center line:81%
A young woman and a leader

01:36.093 --> 01:40.397 align:center line:79%
who were hospitalized for burn treatments
studied the Book of Mormon together.

01:41.231 --> 01:44.601 align:center line:79%
One said, “Lately,
we’ve been reading in Moroni,

01:44.801 --> 01:47.738 align:center line:79%
and Moroni says exactly
what I’ve been feeling. ...

01:48.472 --> 01:50.741 align:center line:81%
When he speaks, it's like he's saying,

01:51.041 --> 01:52.876 align:center line:81%
’You have to learn these words

01:52.876 --> 01:56.780 align:center line:79%
because they are written
for you to help you pass through this.’”

01:58.348 --> 02:01.385 align:center line:79%
At a joint funeral service
for those who perished,

02:01.418 --> 02:05.322 align:center line:79%
Area Seventy Elder Siyabonga
Mkhize counseled,

02:06.123 --> 02:10.861 align:center line:79%
“We should all turn to the Lord at this
time and ask him to comfort our hearts

02:11.561 --> 02:13.830 align:center line:81%
and ... to soothe the pain we feel.”

02:15.298 --> 02:18.468 align:center line:79%
The Young Women President from the
neighboring Leribe

02:18.468 --> 02:21.038 align:center line:79%
Branch, Mampho
Makhura, urged,

02:21.438 --> 02:25.542 align:center line:79%
“Turn to the Lord, and find strength
to accept His will.

02:26.376 --> 02:29.980 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ is ’the author
and finisher of our faith.′

02:30.213 --> 02:33.116 align:center line:81%
Don’t look away, but look to Him.”

02:34.618 --> 02:35.619 align:center line:81%
Look to Him.

02:36.553 --> 02:39.856 align:center line:79%
Her words echo the counsel
of Alma to his son Helaman:

02:40.357 --> 02:42.559 align:center line:81%
“See that ye look to God and live.”

02:43.593 --> 02:48.065 align:center line:79%
Alma cited the experience of Lehi
and his people with the Liahona as a type.

02:49.099 --> 02:51.935 align:center line:79%
“It is as easy to give heed
to the word of Christ,

02:51.935 --> 02:55.739 align:center line:79%
which will point to you a straight
course to eternal bliss,

02:56.239 --> 02:59.576 align:center line:79%
as it was for our fathers
to give heed to this compass,

03:00.010 --> 03:04.014 align:center line:79%
which would point unto them a straight
course to the promised land.”

03:05.015 --> 03:08.819 align:center line:79%
Alma said, “If they would look,
they might live; ...

03:08.819 --> 03:11.888 align:center line:81%
and if we look we may live forever.”

03:13.090 --> 03:15.625 align:center line:79%
On another occasion,
Alma cited the example

03:15.625 --> 03:17.828 align:center line:81%
of the brass serpent raised by Moses

03:18.128 --> 03:21.531 align:center line:79%
when the ancient Israelites
were afflicted by fiery serpents.

03:22.599 --> 03:26.770 align:center line:79%
The Lord told Moses to make a figure
of a serpent and lift it on a pole,

03:27.304 --> 03:29.873 align:center line:79%
with the promise
“that everyone that is bitten,

03:29.873 --> 03:32.809 align:center line:81%
when he looketh upon it, shall live.”

03:34.211 --> 03:38.048 align:center line:79%
Alma explained that the brass
figure was a type or symbol of Christ

03:38.482 --> 03:40.717 align:center line:81%
who would be lifted up upon the cross.

03:41.485 --> 03:45.555 align:center line:79%
Many did look and live,
but others were, in Alma's words,

03:45.555 --> 03:49.326 align:center line:79%
“so hardened” that they simply
would not look and perished.

03:50.393 --> 03:54.831 align:center line:79%
Alma asked: “If he could be healed
by merely casting about your eyes

03:54.831 --> 03:56.199 align:center line:81%
that ye might be healed,

03:56.533 --> 03:58.135 align:center line:81%
would ye not behold quickly,

03:58.869 --> 04:02.873 align:center line:79%
or would you rather harden your hearts
in unbelief and be slothful,

04:02.873 --> 04:06.543 align:center line:79%
that ye would not cast about your eyes,
that ye might perish?

04:07.244 --> 04:11.414 align:center line:79%
“... [T]hen cast about your eyes
and begin to believe in the Son of God,

04:11.414 --> 04:13.950 align:center line:81%
that he will come to redeem his people,

04:13.984 --> 04:17.988 align:center line:79%
and that he shall suffer and die
to atone for their sins;

04:18.421 --> 04:21.057 align:center line:79%
and that he shall rise
again from the dead,

04:21.057 --> 04:23.693 align:center line:79%
which shall bring
to pass the resurrection,

04:23.693 --> 04:28.732 align:center line:79%
that all men shall stand before him,
to be judged at the last and judgment day,

04:29.299 --> 04:30.634 align:center line:81%
according to their works.”

04:32.435 --> 04:36.173 align:center line:79%
Of course, the counsel “Look to
God and live” as meaning for us not only

04:36.173 --> 04:40.877 align:center line:79%
in eternity, but also makes all
the difference in the character

04:40.877 --> 04:42.946 align:center line:81%
and quality of our mortal lives.

04:43.713 --> 04:48.118 align:center line:79%
Remember the words of young Sister Selebei
in Lesotho already mentioned:

04:48.718 --> 04:53.623 align:center line:79%
“Jesus Christ loves us and is with us,
even though our hearts hurt.”

04:55.292 --> 04:58.762 align:center line:79%
It is in the nature of a fallen
world—where the devil rages

04:58.762 --> 05:00.497 align:center line:81%
and where everyone is imperfect—

05:01.231 --> 05:04.334 align:center line:79%
that there will be disappointments
and offenses,

05:04.334 --> 05:11.041 align:center line:79%
suffering and sorrow, failure and loss,
persecution and injustice.

05:11.041 --> 05:15.679 align:center line:79%
It is only by looking
to God that individuals, and families,

05:15.679 --> 05:17.581 align:center line:81%
even nations can flourish.

05:18.615 --> 05:22.853 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson
taught: “Because the Savior,

05:22.853 --> 05:27.357 align:center line:79%
through His infinite Atonement, redeemed
each of us from weakness, mistakes,

05:27.357 --> 05:31.795 align:center line:79%
and sin, and because He experienced
every pain, worry,

05:31.795 --> 05:36.800 align:center line:79%
and burden you have ever had, then
as you truly repent and seek His help,

05:37.400 --> 05:41.004 align:center line:79%
you can rise above
this present precarious world.”

05:43.173 --> 05:47.477 align:center line:79%
No promise is repeated more often
in the Book of Mormon scripture than this:

05:48.612 --> 05:51.047 align:center line:79%
“Inasmuch as ye shall
keep my commandments

05:51.047 --> 05:53.450 align:center line:81%
ye shall prosper in the land:

05:54.251 --> 05:57.220 align:center line:79%
but inasmuch as ye
will not keep my commandments

05:57.220 --> 05:59.522 align:center line:81%
ye shall be cut off from my presence.”

06:00.857 --> 06:02.492 align:center line:81%
The lived experience of the Book

06:02.492 --> 06:07.397 align:center line:79%
of Mormon peoples over centuries
demonstrates the truth of these words.

06:08.531 --> 06:12.802 align:center line:79%
“Prosper” meant enjoying the guidance
and blessing of heaven in their lives.

06:13.603 --> 06:18.475 align:center line:79%
“Prosper” meant achieving levels of
economic well-being that enabled them

06:18.475 --> 06:21.978 align:center line:79%
to marry, raise families, have the
necessities of life

06:22.312 --> 06:24.047 align:center line:81%
(sometimes in abundance),

06:24.848 --> 06:26.983 align:center line:81%
and to minister to the needs of others.

06:27.784 --> 06:31.454 align:center line:79%
“Prospering” included the capacity
to rise above hardship

06:31.454 --> 06:34.524 align:center line:81%
and trial. Through the grace of Christ,

06:34.524 --> 06:38.528 align:center line:79%
all things worked together
for their good, refined them,

06:38.528 --> 06:41.264 align:center line:81%
and deepened their relationship with Him.

06:42.365 --> 06:46.403 align:center line:79%
Alma explained that looking
to God is to keep His commandments,

06:46.403 --> 06:49.172 align:center line:81%
cry unto Him continually for his support,

06:50.206 --> 06:52.442 align:center line:81%
counsel with Him in all your doings,

06:53.243 --> 06:55.812 align:center line:79%
and let your heart be full
of thanks unto Him

06:55.812 --> 06:56.813 align:center line:81%
day and night.

06:58.348 --> 07:01.718 align:center line:79%
God's commandments and counsel
are found in the scriptures

07:01.718 --> 07:03.253 align:center line:81%
and the words of His servants.

07:04.254 --> 07:07.524 align:center line:79%
The principles and ideals
laid out in “The Family:

07:07.557 --> 07:10.593 align:center line:79%
A Proclamation to the World”
are a prime example.

07:11.695 --> 07:15.699 align:center line:79%
Another is the guidance found in
the booklet “For the Strength of Youth.”

07:16.232 --> 07:20.136 align:center line:79%
The Young Men and Young Women
theme for this year is “Look unto Christ,”

07:21.037 --> 07:25.442 align:center line:79%
drawn from the Lord’s comforting direction
to Joseph Smith and Oliver Cowdery:

07:25.442 --> 07:27.277 align:center line:81%
“Look unto me in every thought;

07:27.310 --> 07:28.945 align:center line:81%
doubt not, fear not.”

07:30.080 --> 07:32.015 align:center line:79%
“For the Strength of
Youth” speaks to several

07:32.015 --> 07:34.684 align:center line:81%
of God's most urgent commandments

07:34.684 --> 07:39.856 align:center line:79%
and standards and teaches how to look
to the Lord in making good decisions.

07:40.590 --> 07:43.660 align:center line:79%
It's a guide not only for youth,
but for all of us.

07:44.361 --> 07:49.299 align:center line:79%
As one very important example, “For the
Strength of Youth” has crucial guidance

07:49.299 --> 07:52.335 align:center line:79%
in the chapter titled,
“Your Body is Sacred.”

07:53.236 --> 07:55.271 align:center line:81%
It instructs, “treat your body—

07:55.271 --> 08:00.710 align:center line:79%
and others’ bodies—with respect.
As you make decisions about your clothing,

08:01.311 --> 08:03.680 align:center line:81%
hairstyle, and appearance,

08:03.713 --> 08:09.085 align:center line:79%
ask yourself, ’Am I honoring
my body as a sacred gift from God?’”

08:10.253 --> 08:12.188 align:center line:79%
“For the Strength of Youth” further
states,

08:12.188 --> 08:15.658 align:center line:81%
“Keep sex and sexual feelings sacred.

08:16.192 --> 08:20.363 align:center line:79%
They should not be the subject
of jokes or entertainment. Outside

08:20.363 --> 08:22.132 align:center line:81%
of marriage between a man and a woman.

08:22.132 --> 08:25.702 align:center line:79%
it is wrong to touch the private,
sacred parts of another’s body

08:25.735 --> 08:29.973 align:center line:79%
even if clothed. In your choices
about what you do,

08:30.240 --> 08:35.178 align:center line:79%
look at, read, listen to,
think, post, or text,

08:35.678 --> 08:42.052 align:center line:79%
avoid anything that purposely arouses
lustful emotions in others or yourself.’”

08:43.286 --> 08:47.690 align:center line:79%
This calls to mind President Nelson’s
recent admonition:

08:48.792 --> 08:53.596 align:center line:79%
“Few things will complicate
your life more quickly than violating

08:53.596 --> 08:55.331 align:center line:81%
this divine law [of chastity].

08:56.232 --> 08:59.402 align:center line:79%
For those who have made covenants
with God, immorality is one

08:59.402 --> 09:02.005 align:center line:79%
of the quickest ways
to lose your testimony. ...

09:03.373 --> 09:07.610 align:center line:79%
The power to create life is the one
privilege of godhood

09:08.278 --> 09:11.815 align:center line:79%
that Heavenly Father
allows His mortal children to exercise.

09:12.715 --> 09:17.287 align:center line:79%
Thus, God set clear guidelines
for the use of this living, divine power.

09:18.321 --> 09:22.625 align:center line:79%
Physical intimacy is only for a man and
a woman who are married to each other.”

09:23.626 --> 09:30.667 align:center line:79%
Continuing President Nelson’s comment,
“Much of the world does not believe this,

09:31.601 --> 09:34.370 align:center line:79%
but public opinion is not
the arbiter of truth.

09:35.171 --> 09:38.208 align:center line:79%
The Lord has declared that no
unchaste person will attain

09:38.208 --> 09:39.342 align:center line:81%
the celestial kingdom. ...

09:40.110 --> 09:42.912 align:center line:79%
If you’ve been unchaste,
I plead with you to repent.

09:43.446 --> 09:47.350 align:center line:79%
Come unto Christ and receive His promise
of complete forgiveness

09:48.051 --> 09:51.387 align:center line:81%
as you fully repent of your sins.”

09:53.156 --> 09:56.159 align:center line:79%
Remember that in the Book
of Mormon promise, the opposite

09:56.159 --> 09:58.394 align:center line:81%
of prosperity was not poverty,

09:58.995 --> 10:01.865 align:center line:79%
it was being cut off from
the presence of the Lord.

10:02.832 --> 10:07.270 align:center line:79%
His presence refers to the influence
of His Spirit in one's life.

10:08.071 --> 10:11.941 align:center line:79%
All are imbued with the Light
of Christ as they come into the world.

10:11.941 --> 10:15.945 align:center line:79%
In addition, some act to be baptized
and receive the gift

10:15.945 --> 10:17.947 align:center line:81%
and added light of the Holy Ghost.

10:18.948 --> 10:20.950 align:center line:81%
He brings inspiration and guidance,

10:21.117 --> 10:25.221 align:center line:79%
enhances and refines one's
native gifts and abilities,

10:25.722 --> 10:30.760 align:center line:79%
and helps to avoid evil influences,
poor decisions, and dead ends.

10:32.028 --> 10:36.032 align:center line:79%
Like you, I know some who once enjoyed
the gift of the Holy Ghost, but who,

10:36.065 --> 10:39.769 align:center line:79%
through failure to keep the commandments
of God, have lost that blessing.

10:40.303 --> 10:42.071 align:center line:81%
One in particular comes to mind

10:42.071 --> 10:46.042 align:center line:79%
whose membership in the Church
had been withdrawn due to transgression.

10:46.543 --> 10:49.812 align:center line:79%
He said that his initial
reaction was to feel offended.

10:49.812 --> 10:52.282 align:center line:81%
He felt judged by imperfect leaders.

10:52.782 --> 10:54.517 align:center line:81%
He knew his conduct had been wrong,

10:54.517 --> 10:58.454 align:center line:79%
but he rationalized it by pointing
to the faults and failings of others.

10:59.422 --> 11:01.824 align:center line:79%
After a while,
he began to feel comfortable

11:01.824 --> 11:06.396 align:center line:79%
in a lifestyle outside the Church
without the obligation of callings,

11:06.596 --> 11:10.366 align:center line:79%
expectations of attending worship
services and ministering to others.

11:11.234 --> 11:12.902 align:center line:81%
This continued for some time,

11:12.902 --> 11:18.041 align:center line:79%
but he began to feel ever more
keenly the absence of the Holy Spirit—

11:18.041 --> 11:20.276 align:center line:81%
God’s presence—in his life.

11:21.144 --> 11:25.682 align:center line:79%
By experience, he knew what it was like
to have, day by day, the comfort,

11:25.715 --> 11:28.952 align:center line:79%
guidance, and confidence born
of the Spirit,

11:28.952 --> 11:30.253 align:center line:81%
and he missed it.

11:30.820 --> 11:32.855 align:center line:81%
Finally, he did what was needed to repent

11:32.855 --> 11:37.594 align:center line:79%
and qualify once more
for baptism of water and of the Spirit.

11:39.262 --> 11:44.133 align:center line:79%
There seems to be no end to the different
sources people look to for meaning

11:44.167 --> 11:45.535 align:center line:81%
and happiness and health.

11:46.502 --> 11:48.571 align:center line:81%
Most are “looking beyond the mark.”

11:49.606 --> 11:52.609 align:center line:79%
But we need not be “children,
tossed to and fro,

11:52.609 --> 11:55.979 align:center line:79%
and carried about by every wind
of doctrine [or fashion].”

11:57.180 --> 12:00.316 align:center line:79%
In looking to God,
we can find peace in difficulty

12:01.251 --> 12:04.954 align:center line:79%
and our faith can continue
to grow even in times of doubt

12:04.954 --> 12:06.389 align:center line:81%
and spiritual challenge.

12:07.223 --> 12:11.527 align:center line:79%
We can receive strength
in the face of opposition and isolation.

12:12.462 --> 12:18.134 align:center line:79%
We can reconcile the ideal
with the present reality.

12:18.134 --> 12:23.306 align:center line:79%
Truly, there is no other way than what
God Himself has ordained,

12:24.040 --> 12:28.444 align:center line:79%
“Look unto me, and be ye
saved, all the ends of the earth:

12:29.145 --> 12:32.482 align:center line:81%
for I am God, and there is none else.

12:34.284 --> 12:37.987 align:center line:79%
Looking to God means that He is not
just one of our priorities;

12:39.188 --> 12:42.158 align:center line:79%
it means, rather, that He is
our one highest priority.

12:43.293 --> 12:45.528 align:center line:81%
I call to mind again that awful crash

12:45.528 --> 12:49.265 align:center line:79%
in Lesotho last June.
From her hospital bed,

12:49.265 --> 12:51.801 align:center line:79%
one of the young women
leaders who survived,

12:52.368 --> 12:55.238 align:center line:79%
who did not believe
in God before joining the Church,

12:56.205 --> 13:00.176 align:center line:79%
said that her purpose is now
to discover why her life was spared.

13:01.344 --> 13:03.646 align:center line:79%
“Constantly serving God is how I will
come to an answer,

13:03.646 --> 13:05.915 align:center line:81%
if I come to an answer,”

13:05.915 --> 13:13.589 align:center line:79%
she stated. “I used to think that I love
God, but now I really, really, really,

13:13.589 --> 13:15.124 align:center line:81%
really love Him.

13:16.392 --> 13:19.429 align:center line:79%
Now He is the number
one priority in my life.”

13:21.364 --> 13:23.666 align:center line:81%
I bear testimony of the Father,

13:23.666 --> 13:28.971 align:center line:79%
Son, and Holy Ghost who in perfect
unity of word, thought,

13:28.971 --> 13:34.944 align:center line:79%
purpose, and action are the one God
to whom we may look for all good things.

13:36.112 --> 13:39.182 align:center line:79%
I bear testimony of the Atonement
of Jesus Christ

13:39.582 --> 13:44.520 align:center line:79%
whence comes the power to fulfill
this wonderful promise:

13:45.054 --> 13:50.426 align:center line:79%
“Look unto me, and endure to the end,
and ye shall live; for

13:50.893 --> 13:55.098 align:center line:79%
unto him that endureth to the end
will I give eternal life.”

13:55.732 --> 13:58.368 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

